WEBVTT

00:37:29.482 --> 00:37:30.726
of self-verification;

00:37:30.750 --> 00:37:33.866
Jonathan Evans and colleagues
on self-deprecating jokes;

00:37:33.890 --> 00:37:35.956
Edwin Hollander on idiosyncrasy credit;

00:37:35.980 --> 00:37:39.863
and Alison Fragale, Nate Fast
and colleagues on power without status.

00:37:44.293 --> 00:37:46.503
AG: I hear a lot of leaders
say, "Be authentic!

00:37:46.507 --> 00:37:48.051
Bring your whole self to work!"

00:37:48.075 --> 00:37:50.201
What would you encourage
them to say instead?

00:37:50.225 --> 00:37:51.424
HI: Don't use platitudes.

00:37:51.448 --> 00:37:53.550
That's the first thing
I would say, is don't.

00:37:53.574 --> 00:37:54.725
AG: (Laughs)

00:37:54.749 --> 00:37:57.468
HI: Honestly! Authenticity also
has a sense of uniqueness.

00:37:57.492 --> 00:38:00.318
Everybody and their brother
has said exactly the same thing.